From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wsclean-mx <wsclean-mx@localhost>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:15:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] uvw_file.h: a data row needs a tab, not just a leading
 digit

taql's own header lines can start with a digit ("6 selected columns: u v w xr
xi f0"), so testing only the first character let the header through as a row.
Harmless in the usable count - its v field parses as NaN and is dropped as
non-finite - but it made the row count 621 251 instead of 621 250 and would
have silently absorbed a genuinely malformed first line.

diff --git a/metal/uvw_file.h b/metal/uvw_file.h
index e3aa43f3..5125c152 100644
--- a/metal/uvw_file.h
+++ b/metal/uvw_file.h
@@ -51,7 +51,9 @@ inline RealVisibilitySet LoadUvwFile(const std::string& path) {
   RealVisibilitySet set;
   std::string line;
   while (std::getline(in, line)) {
-    // A data row starts with a number; the header lines do not.
+    // A data row starts with a number and is tab separated; taql's own headers
+    // can start with a digit too ("6 selected columns: ...").
+    if (line.find('\t') == std::string::npos) continue;
     const char* begin = line.c_str();
     char* end = nullptr;
     const double u = std::strtod(begin, &end);
